# Remaining SysON parity work: delivery order and completion criteria

SysON feature parity is still open. Rust foundations and several repairs are on main, but the connected application, complete language and semantic behavior, usable views, durable storage and release qualification still need work. Our next product milestone is a project that a user can create or import, edit, save, reload, reopen and inspect after a backend restart without manually reimporting JSON.

This guide answers three questions: what remains, which PR can proceed next, and what evidence makes it done. The [790-entry task register](remaining-work/units.json) supplies the exact tasks, source paths, dependencies, review budgets and acceptance conditions for every adopted unit. Each entry links to its detailed PR brief. Counts include implementation, generated work and verification; they are neither a feature percentage nor a promise of 790 future PRs.

This execution snapshot is **SYSON-RUST-REMAINING/2026-10-29.15**, based on GitHub main `ef5fe1e797d669bbdc4952a13b9a49b298ab2075` on 2026-10-29. The [completion contract](COMPLETION-CONTRACT.md), version **1.0.7**, defines the required scope. Its [hash lock](completion-contract.lock.json) protects the requirements; the separate [snapshot lock](remaining-work/snapshot.lock.json) binds this guide, task register and progress inputs. The [forest checkpoint](remaining-work/checkpoint-batch26/status.json) preserves the [.14 checkpoint](remaining-work/checkpoint-batch25/status.json) and all earlier attribution. Updating documentation grants no source lease.

The adopted RR08, layout, comparison, partial-field and routing splits preserve the original 778 obligations and add ten execution children. The [forest split](amendments/1.0.7-forest-kernel-split.md) adds U12a/U12b for twelve children and 790 review units. Every parent acceptance gate and F10/F11 disposition remains. Ordinary limits are 400 changed handwritten production lines and 900 authored lines, including tests and coordinator wiring; exceeding an estimate does not waive either cap.

## Current status and the limits of the evidence

Main contains the model, containment, literal JSON, catalogue, history, reference, reflection, value, summary, dispatch, constructor and measurement foundations recorded in [execution.json](execution.json). It also contains the editor padding fix, finite operator component, RR08 selected-copy and journal repairs, their development comparisons, and P01 ordinary line notes. The ledger retains 55 bounded implementation/evidence records, all `NOT_ACCEPTED` for full feature parity. Those historical records keep their original attribution.

The [original .12 checkpoint](remaining-work/editorial-freeze-20261029/status.json) retains its historical base. P01 [#167](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/167) was qualified at that checkpoint with 42 AST/37 adapter checks. Its 25 native/Rust cases include 19 admitted cases and six named restriction/recovery cases, which still require assigned parser work. Profiler #166/#168 and amendment #165/#169 scopes retain their original attribution. None establishes full parent acceptance.

U10a [#171](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/171) and C09a [#172](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/172) are on this snapshot's main. U10a retains 11 public API checks and finite resource ranges; C09a retains 19 focused normal/optimized checks. U10b [#175](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/175) is landed; its actual-main 26 checks plus fmt/Clippy/WASM pass on crate tree `fa12c1312c969adac6f9d30cffe130dec36a28f7`. Its [published profiler #173](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/173) retains finite API ranges and default 1,024-node Work refusals, not successful capacity. C09b1 [#176](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/176) is landed and locally qualified: 19 capture and 20 projection tests pass in both Python modes, with 18 fresh API timing samples. C09b2 [#180](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/180) is landed: fresh actual-main qualification passed 11 tests in normal and optimized Python and all 45 controls on both epochs in both modes. The two earlier failed attempts and exact sources are retained. C01 tool acquisition [#177](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/177) and five-handler version qualification [#178](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/178) are landed; dependency acquisition, build and native application acceptance remain open. The original 686-line prototype remains unexecuted; the reviewed 400-line C09b candidate is rejected after two reproduced false successes and a native-root control admission failure. The old 209-line comparator's seven silent-pass defects also remain evidence. The [new queue](rereview-batch26-next-prs.md) schedules separate bounded repairs.

The RR20/history and borrowed-summary composition in [#130](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/130) remains a locally qualified draft against frozen UI source. Its 151 host cases and 18 release UI recipes apply to that composition. Adoption on main still needs layout, container and routing prerequisites, reconciliation of the optional-graph manifest boundary, and applicable owner handoffs. The 5,442 Rust lines and handwritten loader cannot land wholesale. Keep snapshot branches as evidence inputs and preserve all held registrations.

Implementation, local verification, landing and feature acceptance are separate states. A merged helper does not prove that the default editor calls it; an API sample does not prove responsiveness; a screenshot does not prove a usable workflow. The final section defines the evidence required for each decision.

## Execute the next PRs in this order

Work proceeds in parallel where prerequisites and source ownership permit. Use the [current PR queue](rereview-batch26-next-prs.md) and linked briefs for immediate scopes and complete tasks. The queue orders work; it does not establish readiness. F09–F18 remain legacy prerequisite labels.

1. **Finish U11a resource qualification and publish it separately from its profiler.** The reviewed integer admission source has passed 13 actual public API tests, formatting, Clippy and WASM checks against landed U10b. Measure admitted and refused workloads through that API, retain cancellation and source bindings, and publish the finite tooling and library in separate PRs. U11b starts only after reviewed, landed and locally qualified U11a; it must retain all 16 original tests and demonstrate continued work/cancellation accounting.
2. **Prepare U12a after this amendment lands and an exclusive source lease is issued.** Bind actual U10b. Admit canonical package forests into an opaque token that retains its own spent work and original callback. After U12a is reviewed, landed and locally qualified, U12b consumes that token, gives each sibling-layout call only the remaining budget and debits returned work once. Preserve all 15 original tests and add actual multiple-group exhaustion, late cancellation and atomic-publication checks.
3. **Retain the landed C09 comparison chain when composing callers.** Pin C09a/C09b1/C09b2, preserve both epochs and all refusal controls, and keep the known coordinate fault and ten cases with OPEN dispositions, including restriction/recovery and reference/getter/lifecycle limits. A passing CLI comparison does not accept P01, native lifecycle or the application.
4. **Advance C01 through separate acquisition, execution and application gates.** Anonymous npm acquisition failed with HTTP 401; credential entitlement is unresolved. Preserve that attempt and the independently reviewed monitor repair. The fixed Maven artifact-data acquisition has finished; independently review its captures and publish the finite tooling before proposing any plugin execution. Neither step grants a build, lifecycle-hook, native application, database or UI lease.
5. **Continue independent reference, caller and application preparation.** Close C01/C02 prerequisites, RR08 consuming callers, RR16b/RR17 evidence enforcement and actual-main UI/host/storage reconciliation within their existing scopes. Root owns shared wiring and serializes compiler, native, database and browser execution.

Routing, forest and admitted reference preparation may proceed with disjoint leases. U11b and U12b wait for their own reviewed, landed and locally qualified admission children. Fractional measurement/layout/routing requires a separate reviewed policy. Parser work retains its declared chain; a plan merge does not make P02 or P11 ready automatically.

The [P01 checkpoint](remaining-work/checkpoint-batch23/status.json) retains the earlier `6fd91b9c` attribution. The following repairs and qualification gaps remain relevant at this snapshot:

- **RR08 repair:** #162/#163 charge selected copies, replace whole-state snapshots with nested undo journaling and prevent publication after cancellation or swallowed budget exhaustion. At the RR08 landing, checks passed 42 AST and 27 adapter cases. The original nine regression cases and additional guards remain. This closes the bounded implementation work; actual-parser, native/lifecycle and consuming-caller acceptance remain open under RR08.
- **Operator and constructor qualification:** F12 is on main. Its separate 42-case synthetic callback comparison retains 301 phase observations and 564 open items, with 16 divergence controls. The current constructor report has 80 observations: the original 79 cache differences plus the intentional `outside-comment` admission extension; all 172 open obligations remain. These are observations and obligations, not counts of unique defects. Real text parsing, linking, reference resolution and cache/CST lifecycle still require evidence.
- **Measured improvement:** on the same instrumented Rust API workload and quotas, 5,000-operator apply time changed from 51,351.79–74,517.42 ms to 27.92–29.16 ms; requested allocation traffic changed from 119,619,738,704 to 35,206,832 bytes. The [RR08 performance record](remaining-work/checkpoint-batch22/rr08b-performance-comparison.json) retains all three workload sizes, two warmups/seven measured samples and separate live-heap/RSS accounting. This is the combined RR08a/RR08b repair on a synthetic API workload; it does not establish native, UI or capacity acceptance.
- **Measurement and UI:** the merged developer fixture passes its 14 checks/18 samples at 320/1440 px, but missing CJK/emoji glyphs and synthetic Package/ViewFrame overflow remain open. Actual application measurement/layout/routing, identifier disclosure, dense explorer usability, complete renderer admission and broader accessibility remain unfinished.
- **Durability:** the connected save/reload/reopen/backend-restart milestone remains open. Reconcile #130 and actual host/storage/project prerequisites before transferring any old UI result to main. A helper, DTO, export/reimport loop or local-store test cannot complete that journey.

